<title>2 · The last lawnmower — Sixty Years Later</title>
<meta name="description" content="Lem's second chapter argues that technologies live and die like species — small copying prototypes, radiation into niches, relics in the margins. Sixty years on the pattern holds for machines with a physical niche, fails completely for software, and the disanalogy that matters most is the one he put in a footnote.">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../static/style.css">
<script src="../static/theme.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
<header class="site-header">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="brand" href="../index.html">Sixty Years <span>Later</span></a>
    <nav class="site-nav">
