     3	## 1. The “legislature” indictment is a misread of the unread half of the chapter
     4	
     5	**Location:** “Nothing in the two-evolutions model has a place to put that”; “his frame has only one selection pressure. Everything in the chapter happens by competition in a niche.”
     6	
     7	**Problem:** Two pages after the similarity sentence the essay treats as the thesis, Lem writes that “technical evolution is not, for the time being at least, people-free” and that “the biggest difference” is that bioevolution is “an amoral process, which is something we cannot say about technical evolution” (p. 38). He then spends the rest of the chapter on human agency: moral choice and irreversibility (pp. 47–49), states accelerating or stalling a technology by spending (p. 51), and a civilisation saying “Enough!” and refusing to automatize (p. 57). Regulation as a selector is a 2026 specification of a difference he named and developed. The essay never quotes past “Similarities.”
     8	
     9	**Fix:** Drop or rewrite the “nowhere to put it” claim. If the political selector is the essay’s negative, score it as a problem-level row against p. 38’s “biggest difference” (he named agency; he did not model a legislature that kills the fit and saves the unfit) — not as a hole in a chapter the essay did not read.
    10	
    11	---
    12	
    13	## 2. The air-cushion MISS grades a hedged illustration as a dated forecast
    14	
    15	**Location:** Lede: “he was rash enough to date it”; ledger row: `"further development of mechanical vehicles, which will make wheel drive obsolete"`; “Where he was worst”: “He picked the wrong successor.”
    16	
    17	**Problem:** The governing verbs are “One can also imagine” and “it is quite likely that, say” (p. 36). He gives no year. Two sentences earlier he says cars and aeroplanes “have not yet reached their developmental peak, which is why we cannot talk about their late forms” (p. 35). The lawnmower is a worked example of the relic *pattern*, contingent on a successor that would abolish the wheel. The ledger strips the hedges; the lede invents a dating. Same class of error as scoring a reductio as a forecast (essay 4) and as the hedged entertainment application that had to be pulled from MISS to OPEN (essay 6).
    18	
